{
  "name": "Protect APIs with a Circuit Breaker and Data Tables",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "20e71ff7-5825-4262-a42f-cf4118754c74",
      "name": "Overview Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2200,
        -64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Protect downstream APIs with a circuit breaker using Data Tables\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow implements a reusable circuit breaker for downstream APIs. A check webhook loads the current service state and decides whether a request is allowed. Closed circuits allow traffic, open circuits block calls during a cooldown, and an elapsed cooldown allows one half-open trial. A second webhook records each allowed call as a success or failure. Consecutive failures open the circuit, while a successful call resets the failure counter and closes it.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Create an n8n Data Table named `service_circuits`.\n- Add the fields listed in the **Persist circuit state** section.\n- Select that table in all five Data Table nodes.\n- Set `failure_threshold` and `cooldown_minutes` in **Configure Circuit Breaker**.\n- Publish the workflow.\n- Call `/webhook/circuit-breaker-check` before the downstream API.\n- Continue only when `allow_request` is `true`.\n- Report the outcome to `/webhook/circuit-breaker-result`.\n\n### Requirements\n\nn8n with Data Tables enabled. No external credentials or paid services are required."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9e98050d-1acc-44ea-b1e1-10c4329d94bf",
      "name": "Check API Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1600,
        144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 336,
        "content": "## Check circuit availability\n\nReceives a service key and normalizes the request before evaluating whether the downstream API call should be allowed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4c37cb65-63ec-4418-9d93-9790084efb2c",
      "name": "Result API Note",
